      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "For allowlisted projects, count() on the errors or discover dataset undercounts. A project with only unweighted events returns 0 or NULL. A project with mixed events omits the unweighted ones. Dashboards and Discover results are wrong.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/search/events/datasets/discover.py@sha256:614d74a4ab089a56c12c68ce8dee95e864ed5f5ffa7023a15fe13768a0df5741",
          "source:new:src/sentry/api/helpers/error_upsampling.py@sha256:3d491f2bded087fd5b9e7c3f7dbd31e92b4908b5217bfd960c22cdbf0b4f4a9c"
        ],
        "explanation": "upsampled_count compiles to toInt64(sum(sample_weight)) with no ifNull(sample_weight, 1) fallback. The code comment says sample_weight exists for every event in allowlisted projects, but nothing enforces this. Events stored before upsampling was enabled, or from SDKs that send no client_sample_rate, have a NULL sample_weight. sum() skips NULLs, so those events add nothing. transform_query_columns_for_error_upsampling rewrites every count() to this function whenever all projects are allowlisted. The testutils helper only sets sample_rate when client_sample_rate is truthy, which shows that unweighted events are expected.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 1050,
          "start_line": 1046
        },
